### Background and motivation

This is a proposal to introduce a new gradient brush, `SweepGradientBrush`, also known as conic or angular gradient.

Other frameworks:
* `SweepGradient` in [Android](https://developer.android.com/reference/android/graphics/SweepGradient) and [Flutter](https://api.flutter.dev/flutter/painting/SweepGradient-class.html)
* [conic-gradient](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Values/gradient/conic-gradient) in CSS
* [AngularGradient](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/swiftui/angulargradient) in SwiftUI

This is a prerequisite to support COLRv1 fonts, see the [OpenType specification](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/typography/opentype/spec/colr#sweep-gradients), which is where the proposed name comes from.


### API Proposal

```csharp
namespace System.Windows.Media;

public sealed partial class SweepGradientBrush : GradientBrush
{
    public SweepGradientBrush()
    public SweepGradientBrush(Color startColor, Color endColor)
    public SweepGradientBrush(GradientStopCollection gradientStopCollection)

    public Point Center { get; set; }
    public double StartAngle { get; set; } 
    public double EndAngle { get; set; }

    public static readonly DependencyProperty CenterProperty;
    public static readonly DependencyProperty StartAngleProperty;
    public static readonly DependencyProperty EndAngleProperty;

    // infrastructure (generated)
    protected override Freezable CreateInstanceCore()
    public new SweepGradientBrush Clone()
    public new SweepGradientBrush CloneCurrentValue()
}
```


### API Usage

<img width="738" height="606" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6b79caee-f3c2-41c8-8963-a7bcb65470a0" />

### Alternative Designs

This could be a private brush not accessible to users (which is the case for Direct2D). There is no reason why it shouldn't be public like in the other frameworks; we would like customers to be able to create editors utilizing this brush.

### Risks

I am expecting there to be no possibility of extending the XPS to support a new brush, so it would need to be rasterized on print.

### Background and motivation

Currently WPF does not support horizontal scrolling out of the box. Most of the work had been done in the codebase but it was never publicly surfaced. As a result, ScrollViewer with horizontal scroll bar cannot be scrolled using touch pad.

This is a proposal to add HorizontalWheel events and members mirroring the [Vertical]Wheel ones.

The existing `MouseWheelEventArgs` is reused for both events.

Implementation PR is here: #11956 

### API Proposal

```diff
  namespace System.Windows;

  public class ContentElement
  {
      ...
      public static readonly RoutedEvent MouseWheelEvent;
+     public static readonly RoutedEvent MouseHorizontalWheelEvent;

      public event MouseWheelEventHandler MouseWheel;
+     public event MouseWheelEventHandler MouseHorizontalWheel;

      protected internal virtual void OnMouseWheel(MouseWheelEventArgs e);
+     protected internal virtual void OnMouseHorizontalWheel(MouseWheelEventArgs e)

      ...

      public static readonly RoutedEvent PreviewMouseWheelEvent;
+     public static readonly RoutedEvent PreviewMouseHorizontalWheelEvent;

      public event MouseWheelEventHandler PreviewMouseWheel;
+     public event MouseWheelEventHandler PreviewMouseHorizontalWheel

      protected internal virtual void OnPreviewMouseWheel(MouseWheelEventArgs e);
+     protected internal virtual void OnPreviewMouseHorizontalWheel(MouseWheelEventArgs e)
      ...
  }
```

Same for `System.Windows.UIElement` and `System.Windows.UIElement3D`. 
(`UIElement` has `protected virtual` only handlers)

```diff
  namespace System.Windows.Input

  public static class Mouse
  {
      ...
      public static readonly RoutedEvent MouseWheelEvent;
      public static void AddMouseWheelHandler(DependencyObject element, MouseWheelEventHandler handler);
      public static void RemoveMouseWheelHandler(DependencyObject element, MouseWheelEventHandler handler);

+     public static readonly RoutedEvent MouseHorizontalWheelEvent;
+     public static void AddMouseHorizontalWheelHandler(DependencyObject element, MouseWheelEventHandler handler);
+     public static void RemoveMouseHorizontalWheelHandler(DependencyObject element, MouseWheelEventHandler handler);

      ...

      public static readonly RoutedEvent PreviewMouseWheelEvent;
      public static void AddPreviewMouseWheelHandler(DependencyObject element, MouseWheelEventHandler handler);
      public static void RemovePreviewMouseWheelHandler(DependencyObject element, MouseWheelEventHandler handler);

+     public static readonly RoutedEvent PreviewMouseHorizontalWheelEvent;
+     public static void AddPreviewMouseHorizontalWheelHandler(DependencyObject element, MouseWheelEventHandler handler);
+     public static void RemovePreviewMouseHorizontalWheelHandler(DependencyObject element, MouseWheelEventHandler handler);
      ...
  }
```

Overrides of the new members:

```diff
  namespace System.Windows.Controls.Primitives;

  public class TextBoxBase
  {
+     protected override void OnMouseHorizontalWheel(MouseWheelEventArgs e)
  }
```

```diff
  namespace System.Windows.Controls;

  public class FlowDocumentScrollViewer
  {
+     protected override void OnMouseHorizontalWheel(MouseWheelEventArgs e)
  }

  public class ScrollViewer
  {
+     protected override void OnMouseHorizontalWheel(MouseWheelEventArgs e)
  }
```

### API Usage

`ScrollViewer`, `FlowDocumentScrollViewer` and `TextBox` base start supporting horizontal scrolling without any additional user code required.

Custom handling
```xaml
<Image MouseHorizontalWheel="OnImageHorizontalWheel" ... />
```
```csharp
private void OnImageHorizontalWheel(object sender, MouseWheelEventArgs e)
{
    var delta = e.Delta;
    ...
}
```

### Alternative Designs

A proposed alternative was to add `IsHorizontalMouseWheel` property to the `MouseWheelEventArgs` and not add any new separate events, which is the API in UWP.
However, for WPF this would be a breaking change as existing code would start getting horizontal events and handling them as vertical.

Edit: `HorizontalDelta` was also proposed to lower the compatibility impact while utiliing the existing events. That still carries risks of breaking handlers that do not care about the delta value, or do not expect it to be zero.

Note that `IScrollInfo` already contains `CanHorizontallyScroll` and separate `SetHorizontalOffset`/`SetVerticalOffset` methods so any unification needs to be split by implementations into separate calls anyway. Separate events also correspond to separate `WM_MOUSEWHEEL` and `WM_MOUSEHWEEL` Windows messages.

### Risks

This is mirroring existing events, and implementation is building on existing infrastructure that already has `RawMouseActions.HorizontalWheelRotate`, so existing applications should not be affected.

The only potential risk might be if users already workarounded the gap by handling `WM_MOUSEHWEEL` themselves and did not mark it as handled. The damage would be more or less scrolling than expected.
